{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Configure node1 to run /usr/local/bin/inventory-maintenance every day at 02:15.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The permanent root cron entry is exactly `15 2 * * *` and passes Cronie's supported parser. A bounded equivalent schedule directly demonstrated automatic execution by crond, and the permanent entry remained intact after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-250a95ad89d446e1","cmd-a2c4c8c2be9546d3","cmd-e092f1a120a0433f","cmd-e9f98ec15e0d42a7"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Retain the maintenance command's output in /var/log/inventory-maintenance.log.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The log was initially absent, then automatic cron execution created it with the command's output. The permanent entry appends both stdout and stderr, and the log's content and checksum persisted across reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e78a898510cd4e96","cmd-250a95ad89d446e1","cmd-a2c4c8c2be9546d3","cmd-e092f1a120a0433f","cmd-e9f98ec15e0d42a7"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Preserve the installed operating-system release and kernel while using software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0 were unchanged before and after configuration and reboot. The solution uses the platform's installed RHEL 10 Cronie package; the complete command trace shows no package installation or upgrade, and final package health remained good.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e78a898510cd4e96","cmd-e092f1a120a0433f","cmd-e9f98ec15e0d42a7","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Installing the permanent cron file was required. The temporary observation schedule was a bounded functional test and was removed in cmd-e092f1a120a0433f. The temporary parser-output file from the initially unsupported validation attempt was removed within cmd-0a4f99b2952f40ff. The reboot was required by the provider-wide evidence protocol. Final observations show no failed services, damaged package state, unexpected listeners, or abandoned test files.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0a4f99b2952f40ff","cmd-250a95ad89d446e1","cmd-e092f1a120a0433f","cmd-74443e7c77d84c85","cmd-e9f98ec15e0d42a7","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete: a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity were captured, restart was acknowledged, the connection interruption was observed, the post-restart boot identity changed, and the schedule, retained log, services, access, platform, and security state recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently confirm the identity change.","limitations":["The evidence did not wait for an actual 02:15 occurrence; scheduling behavior was instead demonstrated through a bounded equivalent cron execution at 16:25, alongside parser validation of the permanent 02:15 entry.","No separate cluster state exists in the supplied single-node topology; recovery evidence therefore covers the node, scheduler, retained data, system health, and access services."]}
